.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt BSDTHINKPAD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm bsdthinkpad
.Nd on-screen display for ThinkPad brightness and mute keys
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl i Ar interval
.Nm
.Cm brightness
.Sm off
.Op Cm + | Cm \-
.Ar N
.Sm on
.Nm
.Cm pcm
.Sm off
.Op Cm + | Cm \-
.Ar N
.Sm on
.Nm
.Cm micmute
.Op Cm on | off | toggle
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Without a command,
.Nm
watches the screen brightness, the speaker mute of the ThinkPad embedded
controller and the microphone mute.
It shows a desktop notification when the brightness or the microphone mute
changes, whoever changed it; the speaker mute is shown by the pulseaudio
panel plugin (see below).
It is started with the desktop session by
.Pa @PREFIX@/etc/xdg/autostart/bsdthinkpad.desktop .
.Pp
It reads:
.Bl -tag -width "microphone mute"
.It brightness
.Pa /dev/backlight/backlight0 ,
see
.Xr backlight 9 .
The notification has a bar.
.It speaker mute
the sysctl
.Va dev.acpi_ibm.0.mute ,
see
.Xr acpi_ibm 4 .
The embedded controller mutes the speaker in hardware when the mute key is
pressed, and sends no event.
.Nm
turns the mute LED on and off, which
.Xr acpi_ibm 4
does not.
It also sets the PulseAudio sink mute to match the controller's, at once and
again 150 milliseconds later, so that the pulseaudio panel plugin shows the
speaker mute; it has no notification of its own for it.
The two are independent: where the mute key also reaches the desktop (the X1
Carbon) the plugin toggles the sink with the controller, but the volume keys
unmute only the controller; where it does not (the A475) the sink never
follows on its own.
.It microphone mute
the recording level
.Pq Dq rec
of every mixer that has one, see
.Xr mixer 3 .
A laptop's internal microphone is often a sound device of its own, so all
of them are muted together; the microphone counts as muted when all are.
.Nm
keeps the microphone mute LED in step with it.
.El
.Pp
At start and on every change of the speaker or microphone mute,
.Nm
sets the mute LEDs with
.Xr bsdthinkpad-mute-led 8
through
.Xr pkexec 1 .
If that fails, it warns once and goes on.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl i Ar interval
Poll every
.Ar interval
milliseconds, 50 to 60000 (default 200).
For two seconds after a brightness change it polls every 30 milliseconds, so
that the notification's bar follows the keys or the scroll wheel step by step.
.Pp
When the tpmute kernel module is loaded (the sysctl
.Va hw.tpmute
exists; it reports the speaker mute to
.Xr devd 8 ) ,
.Nm
waits instead: it reads at once on an
.Xr acpi_ibm 4
event from
.Pa /var/run/devd.seqpacket.pipe
and on
.Dv SIGWINCH ,
which the
.Cm brightness
and
.Cm micmute
commands and the panel plugin send it after a change, and otherwise only
every two seconds.
It then reads the speaker mute from
.Va hw.tpmute.state
instead of the embedded controller, and when
.Va hw.tpmute.led
is 1 (tpmute sets the LED itself) it does not set the speaker LED.
.It Fl n
Do not set the mute LEDs.
.El
.Pp
The commands are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm brightness Oo Cm + | Cm \- Oc Ns Ar N
Change the screen brightness by
.Ar N
percent, or set it to
.Ar N
percent without a sign, and print the new value.
Bind the brightness keys to
.Ql bsdthinkpad brightness +10
and
.Ql bsdthinkpad brightness -10 .
.It Cm pcm Oo Cm + | Cm \- Oc Ns Ar N
The same for the OSS
.Dq pcm
level of the default mixer.
PulseAudio sets it together with its volume (the OSS
.Dq vol ) ,
except when it starts: then it restores only
.Dq vol ,
and a low
.Dq pcm
left from before makes everything quiet; the panel plugin has a slider for
it.
.It Cm micmute Op Cm on | off | toggle
Mute
.Pq Cm on
or unmute
.Pq Cm off
the microphone, or toggle it, and print the new state,
.Dq on
or
.Dq off .
Without an argument, only print it.
The mute LED follows through the watcher, or through
.Pa @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-key
for the mic-mute key.
.El
.Pp
The watcher logs to
.Xr syslog 3
with the identifier
.Dq bsdthinkpad :
a failing
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
a failing notification, and, at start, when the kernel can not read the
environment of the process
.Pq Va kern.proc.env ,
which keeps ConsoleKit and so polkit from finding the session.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/devd/bsdthinkpad.conf
.Xr devd 8
rule for the microphone mute key, which arrives only as an ACPI event.
.It Pa @LIBEXECDIR@/bsdthinkpad-key
run by this rule as root: runs
.Ql bsdthinkpad micmute toggle
and sets the LED.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/lib/xfce4/panel/plugins/libbsdthinkpad-plugin.so
the XFCE panel plugin
.Dq ThinkPad Controls .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Make the screen darker by 10 percent:
.Dl $ bsdthinkpad brightness -10
.Pp
Set the OSS pcm level to 100 percent:
.Dl $ bsdthinkpad pcm 100
.Pp
See the messages of the watcher:
.Dl $ grep bsdthinkpad /var/log/messages
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr mixer 3 ,
.Xr syslog 3 ,
.Xr acpi_ibm 4 ,
.Xr bsdthinkpad-mute-led 8 ,
.Xr bsdthinkpad-setup 8 ,
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr mixer 8 ,
.Xr backlight 9
.Sh AUTHORS
.An wugq Aq Mt wugq.dev@gmail.com
